    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4775" root="ثنى" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُنَائِىٌّ</span></b>  [a rel. n. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِثْنَانِ</span>, anomalously formed,
but analogous with other rel. ns. from ns. of
number, as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَاعِىٌّ ثُلَاثِىٌّ</span>, &amp;c., <i>Of,</i> or <i>relating to,
two things</i>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلِمَةٌ ثُنَائِيَّةٌ</span> <i>A word comprising,</i>
or <i>composed of, two letters;</i> as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُمْ</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَمٌ</span>?].
(TA.)

